g rhabdomyolysis onset [Data: Relationships (4419, 65, 2437, 2438); Entities (13779, 13781, 13153)]. Monitoring these biomarkers is essential during 辛伐他汀 therapy, especially when combined with interacting drugs.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Multiple drug classes are contraindicated or hazardous with 辛伐他汀\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Several drug classes pose significant risks when co-prescribed with 辛伐他汀. These include antivirals (奈玛特维/利托那韦), calcium channel blockers (米贝地尔), fibric acid derivatives (纤维酸类衍生物), azole antifungals, macrolide antibiotics, and certain antidepressants (e.g., 萘发扎酮). Structured and unstructured evidence consistently warns that these combinations heighten rhabdomyolysis risk. For example, 米贝地尔 and 纤维酸类衍生物 are explicitly listed in clinical guidelines as substances that, when combined with 辛伐他汀, substantially increase the danger of severe muscle toxicity [Data: Relationships (51511, 51512, 51516, 6175); Entities (11544, 7656, 4966)]. Such contraindications underscore the need for careful medication reconciliation in patients prescribed 辛伐他汀.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Secondary complications include renal failure and reduced therapeutic efficacy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond direct muscle toxicity, 辛伐他汀-related adverse events can cascade into secondary complications. Rhabdomyolysis often leads to 肾衰竭 due to myoglobin-induced tubular obstruction and oxidative damage in the kidneys—a complication noted in multiple clinical reports [Data: Relationships (8603, 18235); Entities (17052)]. Additionally, certain co-administered substances, such as vitamin E, can paradoxically reduce 辛伐他汀’s lipid-lowering efficacy by accelerating its clearance, thereby undermining its therapeutic purpose [Data: Relationships (16331); Entities (17664)]. These dual risks—loss of efficacy and gain of toxicity—highlight the delicate balance required in managing patients on statin therapy.\"\n        }\n    